{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794679714,"nonce":"yOibBhF5xfrOS26CzfVMm5hPiTw=","message":"Reflaxe against the exporter and genhl, 2026-11-14. Same NUC, Haxe 4.3.6, Reflaxe 4.0.0-beta, one pinned P-core, 7 interleaved reps in one session, HL typing for every arm. Mean load1 2.9 (another project's builds), so about 5 to 10% noise.\n\nThe Reflaxe arms are a compiler written for this measurement (nothing returned, no files written). \"walk\" visits every node of every function body and writes a 28-byte record, so it is a lower bound for a binary emitter on Reflaxe. \"7 passes\" is Reflaxe's usual expression preprocessors minus MarkUnusedVariables, which throws \"Logic error\" on part of the unit suite.\n\nWall ms, and the cost over typing alone in brackets:\n\n| | hello | unit suite |\n|---|---|---|\n| typing only | 163 | 2619 |\n| `haxe -hl` | 188 (+25) | 3449 (+830) |\n| exporter on std layer, compiler stopped after | 379 (+216) | 5167 (+2548) |\n| exporter, whole | 621 (+458) | 6020 (+3401) |\n| `-lib reflaxe` loaded, no compiler | 467 (+304) | 2938 (+319) |\n| Reflaxe floor (no passes, no emit) | 553 (+390) | 4742 (+2123) |\n| Reflaxe, walk only | 567 (+404) | 4982 (+2363) |\n| Reflaxe, 7 passes | 737 (+574) | 7555 (+4936) |\n| Reflaxe, 7 passes + walk | 757 (+594) | 7862 (+5243) |\n\nReflaxe's own phase on the unit suite: floor 1.7 s, walk +0.24 s, the 7 passes +2.9 s. It processed 6800 functions and about 266k nodes; the exporter writes 8902 functions and 334k nodes, so Reflaxe's numbers are slightly flattering per function.\n\nWhat follows: the macro route has a floor of about 2.1 s here whatever sits on it, 2.5 times genhl's +0.83 s. Reflaxe does not beat the exporter at that floor. It adds the framework load (+0.3 s, even for hello), the preprocessors (+2.9 s), and cannot cache std, which the layer does (hello 621 to 379, unit 6020 to 5167).\n\nCoverage: Zyntax's Reflaxe IR frontend (removed in zyntax 82db446c, recovered from its parent) only compiled user code with std excluded (`--macro exclude('haxe.Log')`) and rejected std constructs (`TSuper`, `$bytes_sizebits`), so it could not be timed on a whole program.\n\nFiles: nuc:~/tast-bench/bench2.sh, rbench/ (the minimal compilers), times2.tsv, rb-phase.log.","files":null}]}